+# Aegis Quantum Domain Hardening
+
+This directory contains scaffolding to harden the quantum domain in Aegis:
+
+- A reproducible container image Dockerfile for quantum workloads (Qiskit / Cirq / PennyLane).
+- A simulator job wrapper and an optional QPU submission helper (IBMQ / Braket stub).
+- Provenance/evidence bundler for quantum runs, with cosign signing helper.
+- An Argo WorkflowTemplate for hybrid sim→QPU workflows.
+- CI workflow to test circuit submissions on a simulator and build/sign artifacts.
+- Metrics exporter for quantum job queue/latency (Prometheus).
+
+Key recommended production practices:
+- Use a dedicated KMS-backed cosign key to sign all quantum artifacts and recorded results.
+- Keep QPU credentials in Vault / ExternalSecrets and never bake into images.
+- Prefer simulator-based CI; real QPU calls should be gated with approvals and cost accounting.
+- Record full provenance for every QPU job (circuit, backend, shots, job id, result, timestamp) and store signed evidence.
+- Rate-limit and queue QPU submissions to avoid unexpected costs; expose cost metrics.
+
+Quickstart (dev):
+1. Build the quantum runner image: docker build -t aegis-quantum-runner:local .
+2. Run a simulator test: python3 ops/quantum/qiskit_job.py --circuit examples/simple_circuit.json --mode=sim
+3. Use Argo (ops/k8s/quantum-workflow.yaml) to run simulated workflows.
+
